# Engineering Principles — Mobile

Write code that is correct by construction. Prefer the type-checker catching bugs over tests over humans.

These principles are carried from the main monorepo's `engineering-principles.mdc` and adapted for the RN / TypeScript-only context.

## Types First

- Define or update types/interfaces BEFORE writing logic
- Use enums/discriminated unions for domain concepts (status, currency, payment type) — never raw strings
- Make invalid states unrepresentable: if it type-checks, it's valid
- Exhaustive matching — no catch-all `default:` that silently swallows new variants
- Use `never` returns in default branches of exhaustive matches to force compile errors when enums grow

```ts
function statusColor(s: TradeStatus): string {
  switch (s) {
    case 'initiated': return 'blue';
    case 'funded':    return 'amber';
    case 'completed': return 'green';
    case 'cancelled': return 'gray';
    case 'disputed':  return 'red';
    default:
      const _exhaustive: never = s;
      return _exhaustive;
  }
}
```

## Error Handling

- Every error path must be explicitly handled — no swallowing errors
- Every `await fetch()` and every Promise chain handles both success and error
- No empty `catch {}` — every catch does something (log, surface, rethrow)
- Design errors as typed discriminated unions, not strings:

```ts
type ApiError =
  | { kind: 'network' }
  | { kind: 'unauthorized' }
  | { kind: 'validation', fields: Record<string, string> }
  | { kind: 'server',  status: number, message: string };
```

- All errors get logged to Sentry with breadcrumbs
- User-facing errors are friendly, never raw stack traces

## Auth & Security

- Every screen loading user-specific data MUST verify the user is authorized for THAT resource — not just authenticated
- Token storage: `expo-secure-store` ONLY. Never `AsyncStorage`. Never a wrapper. See `no-asyncstorage-for-secrets.mdc`.
- Biometric re-auth required before: withdraw, change password, disable 2FA, delete account
- Cert pinning enabled in production builds (MOBILE-SEC-001)
- Screen capture protection on sensitive screens (MOBILE-SEC-002)

## Frontend ↔ Backend Contract

The backend (`qictrader-backend-rs`) uses `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]` — Rust `snake_case` fields become `camelCase` in JSON.

- When sending data TO the backend, map your variable names to the backend's expected `camelCase` names (e.g. `type` → `offerType`, `type` → `paymentType`)
- When receiving data FROM the backend, map `camelCase` back to local names
- Always check the backend Rust struct definition before writing API calls:
  - Models: `/Users/jpvanzyl/Workspaces/Qictrader/qictrader-backend-rs/src/models/`
  - Handlers: `/Users/jpvanzyl/Workspaces/Qictrader/qictrader-backend-rs/src/api/`
- Backend list endpoints may return flat arrays; don't assume `{ items: [...], total }` wrappers

## Pure Logic, Side Effects at the Edges

- Core domain logic (validators, formatters, fee calc) should be pure and testable without IO
- Push side effects (API calls, native modules, navigation) to the boundaries (screens, hooks)
- Immutable by default
- Avoid `let mut`-style assignments in business logic — use `const` and derive

## Testing

- Tests make real assertions about specific values — not just "did not crash"
- NEVER `not.toBe(404)` — assert `toBe(200)`
- NEVER `toBeDefined()` alone — assert the expected value
- NEVER `if (!res.ok) { return }` — that's a silent pass
- Empty `catch {}` in tests is forbidden
- E2E (Maestro) > component tests (RNTL) > unit tests
- Tests must be independent; no shared mutable state between `it()` blocks

## Design System

All UI work follows `DESIGN.md` (synced from the main monorepo via `scripts/sync-from-web.sh`):

- Poppins font only (weights 400–700). No other font families.
- Brand blue `#00A3F6` via the design-token constant `colors.brand`. No hardcoded hex.
- Spacing, radius, shadow scales from `design-tokens.json` — no magic numbers in components
- NativeWind classes map to the same Tailwind tokens as web — `bg-brand`, `text-foreground`, `rounded-lg` work identically
- Check the anti-patterns section in `DESIGN.md` before writing any markup

## Commit Discipline

- One logical change per commit
- Commit message: `MOBILE-XXX-NNN: short summary` matching the Trello ticket
- Build passes before pushing — no "fix build" follow-up chains
- Never include secrets in commits
- Run pre-push secret-scan and `let _ =` ban scan (see `AGENTS.md`)
